  "names": {
    "en": "Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice",
    "ja": "SEKIRO: SHADOWS DIE TWICE"
  },
  "summaries": {
    "en": "Deflect timing, Posture management, Skill unlocks, and boss-by-boss combat breakdowns for Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice.",
    "ja": "弾きタイミング、体幹ゲージ管理、忍術解放、ボスごとの戦闘解説を網羅したSEKIRO攻略ガイド。"
  },
  "category": "soulslike",
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1528360983277-13d401cdc186?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Deflect (L1/LB at the exact moment of attack contact) refills Posture gauge for both Wolf and the enemy—aggressive deflect-counter play breaks enemy Posture faster than dodging, which pauses the Posture recovery timer.",
      "Mikiri Counter is mandatory for all spear and thrust attacks—spam the stomp input (dodge downward) whenever you see a red kanji danger symbol paired with a thrusting animation. Mikiri Counter deals massive Posture damage and is zero-risk on reaction.",
      "Resurrection costs Unseen Aid probability, not a fixed resource—dying with high Unseen Aid probability (above 60%) and using Resurrection is net positive; dying with low probability (below 20%) and using Resurrection is net negative. Check the Unseen Aid percentage before committing to a Resurrection.",
      "Spirit Emblems gate Prosthetic Tool usage—never spend more than 50% of your Spirit Emblem stock in a single fight; refill from merchants or exploration before each major boss attempt.",
      "Dragonrot progresses when you die without Resurrection (True Death)—cure it periodically using Dragon's Blood Droplets to maintain NPC questlines and Unseen Aid probability above 30%."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "弾き（攻撃接触の正確なタイミングでL1/LB）は狼と敵の両方の体幹ゲージを回復させる。回避は体幹回復タイマーを一時停止させるが、積極的な弾き返しは敵の体幹を回避より速く崩せる。",
      "見切りは全ての槍と突き攻撃に必須。赤い漢字の危マークと突き攻撃アニメーションを確認したらその場でストンプ入力を押す（回避を下に）。見切りは大きな体幹ダメージを与えて、リアクティブにゼロリスク。",
      "甦りは冥助確率を消費し、固定リソースではない。高い冥助確率（60%以上）での死亡と甦りの使用はネットポジティブ。低確率（20%以下）での甦りはネットネガティブ。甦りを使う前に冥助パーセンテージを確認する。",
      "霊気玉は義手忍具の使用を制限する。1回の戦闘で霊気玉ストックの50%以上を使わない。主要ボス挑戦前に商人や探索で補充する。",
      "竜咳は甦りなしで死亡した時（真の死）に進行する。NPCのクエストラインと冥助確率を30%以上に保つため、竜血の雫で定期的に治療する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Ashina Outskirts Priority Route",
        "body": "The opening area introduces deflect mechanics against Ashina soldiers before the first major boss (Gyoubu). Spend at least 30 minutes practising deflect timing against the Ashina Soldier near the Outskirts Wall gatehouse—this enemy's horizontal sweep and overhead attack cover the two most common deflect angles. Unlock Whirlwind Slash (skill tree: Combat Arts) before Gyoubu; it is the highest-damage Art available early and breaks Gyoubu's Posture significantly faster than raw attacks."
      },
      {
        "title": "Early Skill Priority",
        "body": "Mikiri Counter is the first mandatory skill—purchase it from the Skill Menu immediately upon entering the game (it costs 1 Skill Point, available from killing the miniboss at the Outskirts Wall). After Mikiri Counter, prioritise: Whirlwind Slash (damage), Run and Slide (mobility), and Emma's Medicine: Potency (additional healing). Avoid Prosthetic Art upgrades until the third area—Prosthetic Upgrades require materials not available before Senpou Temple."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Genichiro Three-Phase Strategy",
        "body": "Genichiro is the gatekeeping boss that teaches the complete Sekiro combat system. Phase 1 and 2 are deflect-focused: stay in close and deflect every attack rather than creating distance. Phase 3 (Lightning of Tomoe) reverses the dodge instinct—jumping over lightning attacks and countering with the Ascending Carp jump attack deals Posture damage while absorbing the lightning charge. The jump-counter (Lightning Reversal) is mandatory to learn; dodging lightning in Phase 3 deals heavy HP damage instead."
      },
      {
        "title": "Prosthetic Tool Integration",
        "body": "The Shinobi Firecracker (Prosthetic Tool) staggers most non-boss enemies and several mid-boss variants, creating a free deflect-free punish window. Use Firecracker against: Guardian Ape (covers the fart attack approach), Lone Shadow Masanaga (disrupts jump attacks), and Armoured Warrior (breaks guard stance). Never use Firecracker as a primary damage tool—use it as a Posture stagger tool and convert the stagger window into heavy attack sequences."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Isshin Ashina and True Immortality",
        "body": "Isshin Sword Saint (true final boss in one route) has 3 phases of increasing speed and range. Phase 1 (spear): deflect the spear slash, punish the recovery. Phase 2 (double katana): maintain tight range to avoid the charged sweep. Phase 3 (lightning): use Lightning Reversal on every blue-charged attack. The key pattern shift between phases is range management—Isshin extends his safe zone with each phase transition; correspondingly reduce your own punish window from 3-hit to 1-hit finishers to avoid catching his counter-attack start-up."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Dodging backwards against attacks rather than deflecting—backward dodge pauses Posture recovery and loses offensive tempo; all attacks in Sekiro have a deflect window and deflect is always higher value than safe dodging.",
      "Fighting enemies with passive patience—Sekiro rewards aggression; taking 5+ seconds without attacking resets enemy Posture gauge back toward zero, wasting accumulated Posture damage.",
      "Using Gourd Seeds for HP restoration instead of Posture management—Gourd Seeds increase healing capacity but survivability depends on never needing heals; invest Gourd Seeds late when combat competency reduces damage taken.",
      "Attempting Headless and Shichimen Warrior fights without Pacifying Agent or Divine Confetti—these enemy types deal Terror status damage that kills in under 10 seconds without the correct countermeasure items.",
      "Saving Spirit Emblems for \"important\" fights and running out mid-boss—always buy Spirit Emblems from merchants to maintain 30+ stock before major boss rooms."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "攻撃に対して後ろに回避する代わりに弾きを行わない。後退回避は体幹回復を一時停止し攻撃テンポを失う。SEKIROの全攻撃には弾きウィンドウがあり、弾きは常に安全な回避より高い価値を持つ。",
      "受動的な忍耐で敵と戦う。SEKIROは積極性を報奨する。5秒以上攻撃しないと敵の体幹ゲージがゼロに戻り、蓄積した体幹ダメージが無駄になる。",
      "HP回復の代わりに体幹管理のためにひょうたんの種を使用する。ひょうたんの種は回復量を増やすが生存率は回復を必要としないことに依存する。戦闘能力が上がってダメージを受けにくくなってからひょうたんの種に投資する。",
      "首無し武者と七面武者の戦いに平癒薬または聖鈴金紙なしで挑む。これらの敵タイプは適切な対策アイテムなしで10秒以内に殺す恐怖状態ダメージを与える。",
      "霊気玉を「重要な」戦闘のために温存して中ボス戦途中で使い果たす。常に商人から霊気玉を購入して主要ボスルーム前に30個以上のストックを維持する。"
    ]
  },
